{"match_id": "session_2026-09-28-resea-REF-01012-MOB", "source_ref": "REF-01012", "target_population": "MOB", "study_population": "No participants: a national statutory building regulation, not a study", "match_grade": "PARTIAL", "mismatch_note": "Per the 2026-09-25 owner ruling (facility-audit population grading does not turn on participants/auditors; grade on who is served and what was measured): the regulation's own text grounds its minimum-width provision explicitly in wheelchair use, and its gradient/landing/handrail provisions are all MOB-serving by clear intent. The measurement is one step removed -- a legal maximum, not an observation of a disabled person negotiating a ramp -- matching REF-01006/REF-01007/REF-01009/REF-01011/REF-01010's PARTIAL precedent for code/audit sources on this parameter.", "created_at": "2026-09-28 19:49", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-28-research-batch-22-selection", "ref_id": "REF-01012"}
{"match_id": "session_2026-09-28-resea-REF-01013-MOB", "source_ref": "REF-01013", "target_population": "MOB", "study_population": "No participants: a provincial statutory building regulation, not a study", "match_grade": "PARTIAL", "mismatch_note": "Per the 2026-09-25 owner ruling (grade on who is served and what was measured, not on participants/auditors): the clause is explicitly scoped to 'a barrier-free path of travel', clearly MOB-serving by its own heading and text. One step removed -- a legal maximum, not an observation of a disabled person on a ramp -- matching this parameter's other code-source PARTIAL precedent (REF-01006/07/09/10/11/12).", "created_at": "2026-09-28 19:56", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-28-research-batch-22-selection", "ref_id": "REF-01013"}
{"match_id": "session_2026-09-28-resea-REF-01014-MOB", "source_ref": "REF-01014", "target_population": "MOB", "study_population": "No participants: an international standard committee draft, not a study", "match_grade": "PARTIAL", "mismatch_note": "Per the 2026-09-25 owner ruling: the draft's own text explicitly serves and reasons about wheelchair users and elderly people ('heavy to use especially for elderly people and people in wheelchairs... not suitable for independent use'), clearly MOB-serving by intent and content. One step removed -- a standard's reasoned threshold, not an observation of a disabled person on a ramp. Matches this parameter's code/standard-source PARTIAL precedent.", "created_at": "2026-09-28 19:59", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-28-research-batch-22-selection", "ref_id": "REF-01014"}
{"match_id": "session_2026-09-28-resea-REF-01015-MOB", "source_ref": "REF-01015", "target_population": "MOB", "study_population": "No participants: a national statutory building regulation, not a study", "match_grade": "PARTIAL", "mismatch_note": "Per the 2026-09-25 owner ruling (grade on who is served and what was measured, not on participants/auditors): TGD M is titled 'Access and Use' and its ramped-access-route clause is framed throughout in terms of wheelchair users' strength and control needs, clearly MOB-serving. One step removed -- a statutory maximum, not an observation of a disabled person on a ramp -- matching this parameter's recurring code-source PARTIAL precedent (REF-01006/07/09/10/11/12/13/14).", "created_at": "2026-09-28 20:13", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-28-research-batch-22-selection", "ref_id": "REF-01015"}
{"match_id": "session_2026-09-28-resea-REF-01016-MOB", "source_ref": "REF-01016", "target_population": "MOB", "study_population": "No participants: a national design standard incorporated by reference into statute, not a study", "match_grade": "PARTIAL", "mismatch_note": "Per the 2026-09-25 owner ruling: NZS 4121 is titled 'Design for Access and Mobility' and its ramp clause is explicitly keyed to wheelchair users ('sufficient strength', throughout the standard's introduction and rationale), clearly MOB-serving. One step removed -- a design standard's ceiling value, not an observation of a disabled person on a ramp -- matching this parameter's recurring code-source PARTIAL precedent (REF-01006/07/09/10/11/12/13/14/15).", "created_at": "2026-09-28 20:13", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-28-research-batch-22-selection", "ref_id": "REF-01016"}
{"match_id": "session_2026-09-28-resea-REF-01017-MOB", "source_ref": "REF-01017", "target_population": "MOB", "study_population": "No participants: a national statutory decree, not a study", "match_grade": "PARTIAL", "mismatch_note": "Per the 2026-09-25 owner ruling: Decree 241/2017 is explicitly titled 'on Accessibility of Buildings' and its ramp clause sits within a section governing wheelchair-usable routes (kulkuvaylat), clearly MOB-serving. One step removed -- a statutory maximum, not an observation of a disabled person on a ramp -- matching this parameter's recurring code-source PARTIAL precedent (REF-01006/07/09/10/11/12/13/14/15/16).", "created_at": "2026-09-28 20:18", "created_by_session": "session_2026-09-28-research-batch-22-selection", "ref_id": "REF-01017"}

